{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' TOPOPILOT_SCRIPTING_GUIDE.txt\"","aggregated_output":"TOPOPILOT SCRIPTING GUIDE\n=========================\n\nThis guide describes the current scripting API in TopoPilot2Library. The canonical\nstarting point is:\n\n    TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/ui/script_template.py\n\nCopy that file to a new Python script and edit the two placeholder functions:\n\n    def pipeline(load_path):\n        pass\n\n    def create_view():\n        pass\n\nThe template already imports ParaView and every public TopoPilot node, validates\ncommand-line arguments, creates the session/cache directories, renders an image or\ninteractive view, and renders time-varying data to frames before invoking ffmpeg.\n\n\n1. THE NODE PIPELINE MODEL\n==========================\n\nA TopoPilot pipeline is a directed tree of node objects (or a forest if it has\nmultiple independent loaders).\n\n  * A loader is a root node. It reads a .vti file or a directory containing a time\n    series.\n  * Every other node has exactly one parent, named by parent_node_id.\n  * A compute/operation node transforms its parent's output into another typed\n    result (for example, Scalar -> PersistenceDiagram).\n  * An Embed... node turns a computed result into displayable ParaView geometry.\n  * Only displayable embedding nodes should normally be placed in\n    nodes_to_visualize.\n\nConstruct a child after its parent and pass parent.id, not the parent object:\n\n    scalar = LoadScalarField(load_path=load_path, arrayName=\"pressure\")\n    simplified = PersistenceSimplification(\n        parent_node_id=scalar.id,\n        epsilon=0.05,\n    )\n    diagram = ComputePersistenceDiagram(parent_node_id=simplified.id)\n    diagram_view = EmbedPersistenceDiagram(parent_node_id=diagram.id)\n\nThe node tree checks that the parent's output type is compatible with the child.\nNodes are registered as they are constructed and receive a short string id. If an\nidentical root, or an identical child with the same parent and parameters, already\nexists in the in-memory node tree, TopoPilot reuses its id. Node definitions should\ntherefore remain inside pipeline(), where the template expects to create them.\n\nBranches are allowed. For example, the same scalar node may feed both a scalar\nfield embedding and a contour-tree computation:\n\n    scalar_view = EmbedScalarField(parent_node_id=scalar.id, colormap=\"viridis\")\n    tree = ComputeContourTree(parent_node_id=scalar.id)\n    tree_view = EmbedContourTree(parent_node_id=tree.id)\n\n\n2. EDITING pipeline(load_path)\n================================\n\npipeline() must build the nodes and return exactly four values:\n\n    def pipeline(load_path):\n        # 1. Create one loader/root.\n        scalar = LoadScalarField(load_path=load_path, arrayName=\"pressure\")\n\n        # 2. Chain computation nodes using parent.id.\n        simplified = PersistenceSimplification(\n            parent_node_id=scalar.id,\n            epsilon=0.05,\n        )\n        contours = ComputeIsocontours(\n            parent_node_id=simplified.id,\n            num_contours=12,\n        )\n\n        # 3. End displayed branches with embedding nodes.\n        field_view = EmbedScalarField(\n            parent_node_id=simplified.id,\n            colormap=\"cool warm\",\n        )\n        contour_view = EmbedIsocontours(\n            parent_node_id=contours.id,\n            colormap=\"black body\",\n            tube_radius=1.0,\n        )\n\n        # 4. Select the embeddings that the template will render.\n        nodes_to_visualize = [field_view, contour_view]\n\n        # Optional scalar-bar placement, keyed by an embedding node's id.\n        # Value: ([x, y], relative_length, title)\n        color_bar_info = {\n            field_view.id: ([0.82, 0.15], 0.70, \"pressure\"),\n        }\n\n        # These lists are emitted by the UI code generator as cache-planning\n        # metadata. Keep them in the return signature. In the current script\n        # template they are unpacked but are not otherwise consumed.\n        time_invariant_nodes_to_cache = []\n        normal_nodes_to_cache = []\n\n        return (\n            nodes_to_visualize,\n            color_bar_info,\n            time_invariant_nodes_to_cache,\n            normal_nodes_to_cache,\n        )\n\nImportant details:\n\n  * Always use the load_path argument supplied to pipeline(), rather than hard-coding\n    the input filename. The -i CLI option supplies this value.\n  * A single input is a .vti file.\n  * A time series is a directory named NAME containing NAME1.vti, NAME2.vti, ...,\n    with consecutive one-based numbering and no unrelated directory entries.\n  * Use the exact point-array names stored in the VTI file when constructing a\n    loader. The loaders rename them internally to TopoPilot's standard names.\n  * The nodes_to_visualize order is also the rendering order. Put a background\n    surface/volume before points, contours, or trees that should appear over it.\n  * color_bar_info is optional. Omit an entry for a node that needs no scalar bar.\n    Position uses normalized view coordinates; length is a normalized fraction.\n  * Scalar/contour colormap choices currently are: grey, eigenvector partition,\n    eigenvalue partition, bent cool warm, black body, cool warm, extended kindlmann,\n    fast, inferno, kindlmann, plasma, and viridis.\n\n\n3. EDITING create_view()\n========================\n\ncreate_view() must create and return a ParaView RenderView. Camera and viewport\nsettings belong here, not in pipeline():\n\n    def create_view():\n        view = CreateView(\"RenderView\")\n\n        view.ViewSize = [1280, 720]\n        view.OrientationAxesVisibility = 1\n        view.CenterOfRotation = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]\n        view.CameraPosition = [0.0, 0.0, 100.0]\n        view.CameraFocalPoint = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]\n        view.CameraViewUp = [0.0, 1.0, 0.0]\n        view.CameraParallelScale = 50.0\n        view.CameraParallelProjection = True\n        view.CameraViewAngle = 30.0\n        view.InteractionMode = \"2D\"\n\n        return view\n\nThe template sets a white background for a single time step after create_view()\nreturns. For video rendering, set any required background properties directly in\ncreate_view(), because the multi-frame branch does not apply that single-frame\nbackground override. Use even ViewSize dimensions for video encoding.\n\nThe TopoPilot UI can generate this function from its current ParaView camera. If\nwriting it by hand, adjust CameraPosition, CameraFocalPoint, CameraViewUp, and\nCameraParallelScale until the data is framed correctly. For a 3D view, use an\nappropriate camera and change InteractionMode (commonly to \"3D\").\n\n\n4. COMPLETE MINIMAL SCRIPT EDIT\n===============================\n\nStarting from script_template.py, the smallest useful replacements are:\n\n    def pipeline(load_path):\n        scalar = LoadScalarField(load_path=load_path, arrayName=\"pressure\")\n        field_view = EmbedScalarField(\n            parent_node_id=scalar.id,\n            colormap=\"viridis\",\n        )\n\n        nodes_to_visualize = [field_view]\n        color_bar_info = {\n            field_view.id: ([0.82, 0.15], 0.70, \"pressure\"),\n        }\n        return nodes_to_visualize, color_bar_info, [], []\n\n    def create_view():\n        view = CreateView(\"RenderView\")\n        view.ViewSize = [1280, 720]\n        view.CameraPosition = [0.0, 0.0, 100.0]\n        view.CameraFocalPoint = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]\n        view.CameraViewUp = [0.0, 1.0, 0.0]\n        view.CameraParallelProjection = True\n        view.CameraParallelScale = 50.0\n        view.InteractionMode = \"2D\"\n        return view\n\n\n5. RUNNING THE SCRIPT\n=====================\n\nRun it in an environment containing TopoPilot, ParaView, and TTK.\n\nSingle VTI to PNG:\n\n    pvbatch my_pipeline.py -i ./data.vti -t 1 -o output.png\n\nSingle VTI interactively:\n\n    python3 my_pipeline.py -i ./data.vti -t 1 -x\n\nAll steps of a time-series directory to MP4:\n\n    pvbatch my_pipeline.py -i path/to/NAME -t -1 -o output.mp4 -q session\n\nOne time step from a time-series directory to PNG:\n\n    pvbatch my_pipeline.py -i path/to/NAME -t 4 -o output.png -q session\n\nCLI options:\n\n  -i PATH   Required .vti file or time-series directory.\n  -x        Interactive mode; cannot be combined with -o, and cannot display a\n            multi-step input with -t -1.\n  -o PATH   Output .png for one step or .mp4 for all steps.\n  -t N      One-based time step; -1 means all steps (default).\n  -q DIR    Session, cache, and temporary-frame directory (default: current dir).\n\nVideo output requires ffmpeg on PATH. The template currently invokes it at 4 fps.\n\n\n6. NODE REFERENCE\n=================\n\nIn every non-loader constructor, parent_node_id is the id of the immediately\npreceding compatible node. Defaults are shown below.\n\n\nDATA LOADERS (ROOT NODES)\n-------------------------\n\nLoadScalarField(load_path, arrayName=\"\")\n    Loads a scalar field. load_path is a VTI or time-series directory. arrayName is\n    the point-data array; it may be empty only when the file has one array.\n\nLoadVectorField(load_path, u_array_name, v_array_name)\n    Loads a 2D vector field from the point arrays holding its x/u and y/v\n    components.\n\nLoadSymmetricTensorField(load_path, A_array_name, B_array_name, D_array_name)\n    Loads a 2D symmetric tensor [[A, B], [B, D]] from three point arrays.\n\nLoadAsymmetricTensorField(load_path, A_array_name, B_array_name,\n                          C_array_name, D_array_name)\n    Loads a 2D general tensor [[A, B], [C, D]] from four point arrays.\n\n\nFIELD EMBEDDINGS\n----------------\n\nEmbedScalarField(parent_node_id, colormap=\"cool warm\")\n    Displays a scalar field as a colored surface (2D) or volume (3D). colormap must\n    be one of the colormap names listed in Section 2.\n\nEmbedVectorField(parent_node_id)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '260,620p' TOPOPILOT_SCRIPTING_GUIDE.txt && sed -n '1,300p' TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/ui/script_template.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '260,620p' TOPOPILOT_SCRIPTING_GUIDE.txt && sed -n '1,300p' TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/ui/script_template.py\"","aggregated_output":"EmbedVectorField(parent_node_id)\n    Displays a vector field using its geometric vector-field embedding.\n\nEmbedSymmetricTensorField(parent_node_id)\n    Displays a symmetric tensor field using its geometric tensor embedding.\n\nEmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvectorPartition(parent_node_id, resolution=16)\n    Displays the asymmetric-tensor domain partitioned by eigenvector behavior.\n    resolution is the number of subdivisions per grid cell; higher is slower and\n    smoother.\n\nEmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvaluePartition(parent_node_id, resolution=16)\n    Displays regions dominated by scaling, rotation, or anisotropic stretching,\n    including direction where applicable. resolution controls subdivisions per\n    grid cell.\n\n\nSCALAR OPERATIONS AND TOPOLOGICAL STRUCTURES\n--------------------------------------------\n\nPersistenceSimplification(parent_node_id, epsilon)\n    Simplifies a scalar field. epsilon is a fraction of the function range: 0 means\n    no simplification and 1 spans the entire range.\n\nComputePersistenceDiagram(parent_node_id)\n    Computes a scalar field's persistence diagram.\n\nEmbedPersistenceDiagram(parent_node_id, ball_radius=0.02, tube_radius=0.01)\n    Displays persistence pairs as balls and tubes. Both radii are fractions of the\n    scalar function range.\n\nComputeMorseSmaleSegmentation(parent_node_id)\n    Computes the Morse-Smale segmentation of a scalar field.\n\nEmbedMorseSmaleSegmentation(parent_node_id)\n    Creates displayable geometry for a Morse-Smale segmentation.\n\nComputeIsocontours(parent_node_id, num_contours)\n    Computes num_contours isovalues uniformly across a scalar field's value range.\n\nEmbedIsocontours(parent_node_id, colormap=\"cool warm\", tube_radius=1.0)\n    Displays isocontours with the selected colormap. tube_radius is the contour tube\n    radius used for 2D data.\n\nComputeContourTree(parent_node_id)\n    Computes a scalar field's contour tree.\n\nEmbedContourTree(parent_node_id, ball_radius=3.0, tube_radius=1.5,\n                 color_scheme=[\"#002fff\", \"#758fff\", \"#ffdee7\", \"#ff0046\",\n                               \"#000000\"])\n    Displays contour-tree vertices and edges. ball_radius and tube_radius size the\n    geometry. color_scheme must contain five hex colors for minima, 1-saddles,\n    2-saddles, maxima, and degenerate points, in that order.\n\nComputeMergeTree(parent_node_id, which_tree=\"join\")\n    Computes a merge tree. which_tree must be \"join\" or \"split\".\n\nEmbedMergeTree(parent_node_id, ball_radius=3.0, tube_radius=1.5,\n               color_scheme=[\"#002fff\", \"#758fff\", \"#ffdee7\", \"#ff0046\",\n                             \"#000000\"])\n    Displays merge-tree vertices and edges. Parameters have the same meanings and\n    color order as EmbedContourTree.\n\n\nFIELD-TO-FIELD OPERATIONS\n-------------------------\n\nVectorFieldMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a vector field to a scalar magnitude field.\n\nSymmetricTensorMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a symmetric tensor field to a scalar magnitude field.\n\nAsymmetricTensorMagnitude(parent_node_id)\n    Converts an asymmetric tensor field to a scalar magnitude field.\n\nScalarGradient(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a scalar field to its vector gradient field.\n\nVectorGradient(parent_node_id)\n    Converts a vector field to its asymmetric-tensor gradient/Jacobian field.\n\n\nPOINT COMPUTATION AND EMBEDDING\n-------------------------------\n\nComputeScalarCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, which_points)\n    Computes selected critical points of a scalar field. which_points must be one\n    of these exact strings:\n      - \"all critical points (mins+maxes+saddles)\"\n      - \"minima\"\n      - \"maxima\"\n      - \"saddles\"\n      - \"all contour tree vertices (mins+maxes+saddles)\"\n      - \"contour tree saddles\"\n\nComputeVectorCriticalPoints(parent_node_id)\n    Computes critical points of a vector field.\n\nComputeSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id)\n    Computes degenerate points of a symmetric tensor field.\n\nComputeAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id)\n    Computes degenerate points of an asymmetric tensor field.\n\nEmbedScalarCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n                          color_scheme=[\"#3b4cc0\", \"#aac7fd\", \"#f7b89c\",\n                                        \"#b40426\", \"#000000\"])\n    Displays scalar critical points as spheres. radius controls sphere size.\n    color_scheme contains five hex colors for minima, index-1 saddles, index-2\n    saddles, maxima, and degenerate points.\n\nEmbedVectorCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n                          color_scheme=[\"#9d2c00\", \"#f0c571\", \"#0b81a2\",\n                                        \"#e25759\", \"#7e4794\", \"#59a89c\"])\n    Displays vector critical points as spheres. The six colors represent sources,\n    saddles, sinks, source spirals, centers, and sink spirals.\n\nEmbedSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n                                     color_scheme=[\"#ffffff\", \"#ff8cc6\"])\n    Displays symmetric-tensor degenerate points. The two colors represent\n    trisectors and wedges; radius controls sphere size.\n\nEmbedAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0,\n                                      color_scheme=[\"#ffffff\", \"#ff8cc6\"])\n    Displays asymmetric-tensor degenerate points. The two colors represent\n    trisectors and wedges; radius controls sphere size.\n\n\nPOINT TRACKING AND TRACKED-POINT EMBEDDING\n------------------------------------------\n\nTracking requires a time-series root. For each Track... node, time_steps is a\npositive number of steps or -1 for every available step. backend must be \"emd\",\n\"sinkhorn\", or \"partial\".\n\nTrackScalarCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, time_steps, backend)\n    Tracks scalar critical points over time.\n\nTrackVectorCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, time_steps, backend)\n    Tracks vector critical points over time.\n\nTrackSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, time_steps, backend)\n    Tracks symmetric-tensor degenerate points over time.\n\nTrackAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, time_steps, backend)\n    Tracks asymmetric-tensor degenerate points over time.\n\nEmbedTrackedScalarFieldCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0)\n    Displays tracked scalar critical points, colored by tracked identity. radius\n    controls sphere size.\n\nEmbedTrackedVectorFieldCriticalPoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0)\n    Displays tracked vector critical points, colored by tracked identity.\n\nEmbedTrackedSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0)\n    Displays tracked symmetric-tensor degenerate points, colored by identity.\n\nEmbedTrackedAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_node_id, radius=3.0)\n    Displays tracked asymmetric-tensor degenerate points, colored by identity.\n\n\n7. COMMON CHAIN PATTERNS\n========================\n\nScalar field and persistence diagram:\n\n    scalar = LoadScalarField(load_path, \"pressure\")\n    simplified = PersistenceSimplification(scalar.id, 0.05)\n    field_view = EmbedScalarField(simplified.id, \"viridis\")\n    pd = ComputePersistenceDiagram(simplified.id)\n    pd_view = EmbedPersistenceDiagram(pd.id)\n    nodes_to_visualize = [field_view, pd_view]\n\nVector magnitude displayed as a scalar:\n\n    vector = LoadVectorField(load_path, \"u\", \"v\")\n    magnitude = VectorFieldMagnitude(vector.id)\n    magnitude_view = EmbedScalarField(magnitude.id, \"inferno\")\n\nTracked scalar critical points:\n\n    scalar = LoadScalarField(load_path, \"pressure\")\n    critical = ComputeScalarCriticalPoints(scalar.id, \"maxima\")\n    tracked = TrackScalarCriticalPoints(critical.id, -1, \"sinkhorn\")\n    tracked_view = EmbedTrackedScalarFieldCriticalPoints(tracked.id, radius=3.0)\n\nAsymmetric-tensor eigenvalue partition:\n\n    tensor = LoadAsymmetricTensorField(load_path, \"A\", \"B\", \"C\", \"D\")\n    partition_view = EmbedAsymmetricTensorFieldEigenvaluePartition(\n        tensor.id,\n        resolution=32,\n    )\n\n\n8. PRACTICAL CHECKLIST\n======================\n\n  1. Copy script_template.py; do not remove its imports or CLI/rendering body.\n  2. Implement pipeline(load_path).\n  3. Begin each branch with the correct loader and exact VTI array names.\n  4. Pass parent.id into every child node and keep node types compatible.\n  5. End every displayed branch with an Embed... node.\n  6. Return the four required pipeline values.\n  7. Implement create_view() and return the RenderView.\n  8. Test one time step to PNG before rendering an entire MP4.\n  9. If geometry is missing, first verify array names, nodes_to_visualize, camera\n     position/focal point, and the selected time step.\nfrom paraview.simple import *\nfrom topopilot.nodes import *\nimport topopilot.config as config\nimport topopilot.nodeTree as tree\nimport argparse\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nDEFAULT_RANDOM_SEED = 0\n\ndef pipeline(load_path):\n    pass\n\ndef create_view():\n    pass\n\ndef validate_arguments(args):\n    if args.i[-4:] == \".vti\":\n        time_steps = 1\n    else:\n        if not os.path.isdir(args.i):\n            print(\"error: file specified with -i must either be .vti file or directory\")\n            exit(1)\n        \n        time_steps = len(os.listdir(args.i))\n        \n        basename = os.path.basename(args.i)\n        dirname = os.path.dirname(args.i)\n\n        for i in range(1,time_steps+1):\n            \n            if not os.path.isfile(f\"{dirname}/{basename}/{basename}{i}.vti\"):\n                print(\"error: invalid input format for directory\")\n                print(f\"missing file {dirname}/{basename}/{basename}{i}.vti\")\n                exit(1)\n        \n    if args.t > time_steps:\n        print(\"error: time step is too high\")\n        exit(1)                             \n\n    if args.x and args.t == -1 and time_steps > 1:\n        print(\"error: cannot run interactive mode on multiple time steps\")\n        exit(1)\n                                    \n    if args.o != \"\" and args.x:\n        print(\"error: you cannot specify an output file and -interactive\")\n        exit(1)\n    \n    if args.o == \"\" and not args.x:\n        print(\"error: you must either specify an output file or run in interactive mode.\")\n        exit(1)\n                                    \n    if args.t == -1 and time_steps > 1 and args.o[-4:] != \".mp4\":\n        print(\"error: when outputting to video format your output filename must end in .mp4\")\n        exit(1)\n    \n    if args.t != -1 and not args.x and args.o[-4:] != \".png\":\n        print(\"error: when outputting to image format your output filename must end in .png\")\n        exit(1)\n                                    \n    if args.t == -1 and time_steps == 1:\n        args.t = 1\n\n    return time_steps\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"User generated scientific visualization pipeline. Generates images or videos based on user input.\")\n\n    parser.add_argument(\"-i\", help=\"The file that should be loaded.\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-x\", help=\"Should you load into interactive mode? (no images will be generated)\", action=argparse.BooleanOptionalAction)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-o\", help=\"The name of the file that we are outputting.\", default=\"\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"-t\", help=\"What time step should be loaded. Put -1 to generate a video of all time steps. If the data only has one time step, -1 will just load the one time step.\", type=int, default=-1)\n    parser.add_argument(\"-q\", help=\"What folder should be used for temporary files\", default=\".\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--seed\", help=\"Seed for TopoPilot-owned random colors and identifiers.\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_RANDOM_SEED)\n\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    time_steps = validate_arguments(args)\n\n    config.set_random_seed(args.seed)\n    config.change_session_folder(args.q)\n\n    sessionDir = Path(f\"{config.session_folder()}\")\n    sessionDir.mkdir(exist_ok = True)\n    cacheDir = Path(f\"{config.session_folder()}/cache\")\n    cacheDir.mkdir(exist_ok = True)\n\n    nodes_to_visualize, color_bar_info, time_invariant_nodes_to_cache, normal_nodoes_to_cache = pipeline(args.i)\n\n    if args.t != -1:\n\n        renderView = create_view()\n        renderView.Background = [1.0, 1.0, 1.0]\n        renderView.UseColorPaletteForBackground = 0\n\n        for n in nodes_to_visualize:\n            props = n.visualize(args.t, renderView)\n\n            if n.id in color_bar_info:\n                position, length, title = color_bar_info[n.id]\n\n                lut = props.LookupTable\n                bar = GetScalarBar(lut, renderView)\n\n                bar.WindowLocation = \"Any Location\"\n                bar.Position = position\n                bar.ScalarBarLength = length\n                bar.Title = title\n                bar.ComponentTitle = ''\n\n                props.SetScalarBarVisibility(renderView, True)\n\n        if args.o:\n            SaveScreenshot(args.o)\n        else:\n            Interact()\n\n    else:\n\n        for t in range(time_steps):\n\n            renderView = create_view()\n\n            for n in nodes_to_visualize:\n                props = n.visualize(t+1, renderView)\n\n                if n.id in color_bar_info:\n                    position, length, title = color_bar_info[n.id]\n\n                    lut = props.LookupTable\n                    bar = GetScalarBar(lut, renderView)\n\n                    bar.WindowLocation = \"Any Location\"\n                    bar.Position = position\n                    bar.ScalarBarLength = length\n                    bar.Title = title\n                    bar.ComponentTitle = ''\n\n                    props.SetScalarBarVisibility(renderView, True)\n\n            SaveScreenshot(f\"{args.q}/frame{str(t+1).zfill(8)}.png\", renderView)\n\n            Disconnect()\n            tree.clear_evaluation_cache()\n            Connect()\n\n        os.system(f\"ffmpeg -framerate 4 -i {args.q}/frame%08d.png -c:v libx264 -pix_fmt yuv420p {args.o}\")\n\n        for t in range(time_steps):\n            os.remove(f\"{args.q}/frame{str(t+1).zfill(8)}.png\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"which pvbatch && python3 - <<'PY'\ntry:\n import vtk\n print('vtk', vtk.vtkVersion.GetVTKVersion())\n r=vtk.vtkXMLImageDataReader(); r.SetFileName('cylinder/cylinder1.vti'); r.Update()\n d=r.GetOutput(); print('dims',d.GetDimensions(),'bounds',d.GetBounds())\n print([(d.GetPointData().GetArrayName(i),d.GetPointData().GetArray(i).GetNumberOfComponents()) for i in range(d.GetPointData().GetNumberOfArrays())])\nexcept Exception as e: print(type(e).__name__,e)\nPY\nsed -n '1,280p' TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/nodes/pointTrackingNodes.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"which pvbatch && python3 - <<'PY'\ntry:\n import vtk\n print('vtk', vtk.vtkVersion.GetVTKVersion())\n r=vtk.vtkXMLImageDataReader(); r.SetFileName('cylinder/cylinder1.vti'); r.Update()\n d=r.GetOutput(); print('dims',d.GetDimensions(),'bounds',d.GetBounds())\n print([(d.GetPointData().GetArrayName(i),d.GetPointData().GetArray(i).GetNumberOfComponents()) for i in range(d.GetPointData().GetNumberOfArrays())])\nexcept Exception as e: print(type(e).__name__,e)\nPY\nsed -n '1,280p' TopoPilot2Library/src/topopilot/nodes/pointTrackingNodes.py\"","aggregated_output":"import ot\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom paraview.simple import *\n\nfrom .node import Node, ModuleSummary\n\nfrom topopilot.mcp_tools.options import options_lists, enumerate_list\nfrom topopilot.utils.colors import random_hex_colors\nfrom topopilot.config import correctness_checks_on\nimport topopilot.types as types\nimport topopilot.nodeTree as tree\n\ndef _track_points(point_data_list, time_steps, backend):\n    feature_matrices = []\n\n    for t in range(time_steps):\n        points_paraview = PointAndCellIds(Input=point_data_list[t].points)\n        points_paraview.GenerateCellIds = 0\n\n        points_vtk = servermanager.Fetch(points_paraview)\n        numPoints = points_vtk.GetNumberOfPoints()\n        ids_array = points_vtk.GetPointData().GetArray(\"PointIds\")\n\n        feature_matrix = np.zeros((numPoints,3))\n\n        for idx in range(numPoints):\n            point = points_vtk.GetPoint(idx)\n            id_ = ids_array.GetTuple1(idx)\n            feature_matrix[int(id_),:] = point\n\n        feature_matrices.append(feature_matrix)\n    \n    coupling_matrices = []\n\n    for t in range(time_steps-1):\n        \n        feat1 = feature_matrices[t]\n        feat2 = feature_matrices[t+1]\n\n        if backend == \"emd\":\n            emd = ot.da.EMDTransport()\n            emd.fit(Xs=feat1, Xt=feat2)\n            coupling_matrices.append(emd.coupling_)\n        elif backend == \"sinkhorn\":\n            sinkhorn = ot.da.SinkhornTransport()\n            sinkhorn.fit(Xs=feat1, Xt=feat2)\n            coupling_matrices.append(sinkhorn.coupling_)\n        elif backend == \"partial\":\n            C = ot.dist(feat1, feat2)\n            n = len(feat1)\n            m = len(feat2)\n            a = np.ones(n)\n            b = np.ones(m)\n\n            mass = min(n,m)\n\n            T = ot.partial.partial_wasserstein(a, b, C, m=mass)\n            coupling_matrices.append(T)\n\n    feature_pairing = []\n    first_feature = {}\n    num_initial_features = coupling_matrices[0].shape[0]\n    for i in range(num_initial_features):\n        first_feature[i] = i\n\n    next_feat = num_initial_features\n\n    feature_pairing.append(first_feature)\n\n    for t,matrix in enumerate(coupling_matrices):\n        index_pairing = {}\n\n        for i in range(matrix.shape[0]):\n            future_feat = np.argmax(matrix[i,:])\n            if future_feat in index_pairing:\n                if matrix[i,future_feat] > matrix[index_pairing[future_feat],future_feat]:\n                    index_pairing[future_feat] = i\n            else:\n                index_pairing[future_feat] = i\n\n        pairing = {}\n\n        for j in range(matrix.shape[1]):\n            if j in index_pairing:\n                pairing[j] = feature_pairing[t][index_pairing[j]]\n            else:\n                pairing[j] = next_feat\n                next_feat += 1\n        \n        feature_pairing.append(pairing)\n\n    return feature_pairing\n\ndef _generate_color_list(tracking_steps):\n    max_tracking_id = max([ max(d.values()) for d in tracking_steps ])\n    return random_hex_colors(max_tracking_id + 1, \"point-tracking-colors\")\n\nclass TrackScalarCriticalPoints(Node):\n\n    def __init__(self, parent_node_id : str, time_steps : int, backend : str):\n        if correctness_checks_on():\n            if not tree.has_node(parent_node_id):\n                raise Exception(f\"There is no node with id {parent_node_id}\")\n\n            if backend not in options_lists[\"tracking\"]:\n                raise Exception(f\"Invalid tracking backend {backend}. Valid choices are {enumerate_list(options_lists['tracking'])}\")\n            parent_time_steps = tree.node(parent_node_id).root_node.time_steps\n            if time_steps == 0 or time_steps < -1 or time_steps > parent_time_steps:\n                raise Exception(f\"Invalid number of time steps. Must be between 1 and {parent_time_steps} or -1 for all time steps.\")\n\n        super().__init__(parent_node_id, types.ScalarCriticalPoints, types.TrackedScalarCriticalPoints, locals(), True, True)\n\n        if time_steps == -1:\n            self.time_steps = self.root_node.time_steps\n        else:\n            self.time_steps = time_steps\n        self.backend = backend\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"queued tracking scalar field critical points\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def description(cls):\n        return 'Tracks the locations of scalar field critical points over time.'\n\n    @classmethod\n    def param_descriptions(cls):\n        return {'parent_node_id': 'The id of a node of type scalar_cp corresponding to the points that are tracked.',\n            'time_steps': 'How many time steps should the tracking be computed for. Set this to -1 for all time steps.',\n         'backend': 'Which backend algorithm should be used for the tracking. Choices are '\n                    'OPTIONS:tracking.'}\n\n    @classmethod\n    def mandatory_parameters(cls):\n        return [\"time_steps\", \"backend\"]\n    \n    def _evaluation_logic(self, parent_data, time_step):\n        pairing = _track_points(parent_data, self.time_steps, self.backend)\n        return types.TrackedScalarCriticalPoints(parent_data[time_step-1].points, pairing)\n    \n    def _evaluation_logic_partial_cache(self, parent_data, partial_cache, time_step):\n        partial_cache.points = parent_data.points\n        return partial_cache\n\nclass TrackVectorCriticalPoints(Node):\n\n    def __init__(self, parent_node_id : str, time_steps : int, backend : str):\n\n        if correctness_checks_on():\n            if not tree.has_node(parent_node_id):\n                raise Exception(f\"There is no node with id {parent_node_id}\")\n\n            if backend not in options_lists[\"tracking\"]:\n                raise Exception(f\"Invalid tracking backend {backend}. Valid choices are {enumerate_list(options_lists['tracking'])}\")\n            if time_steps == 0 or time_steps < -1 or time_steps > tree.node(parent_node_id).root_node.time_steps:\n                raise Exception(f\"Invalid number of time steps. Must be between 1 and {tree.node(parent_node_id).root_node.time_steps} or -1 for all time steps.\")\n\n        super().__init__(parent_node_id, types.VectorCriticalPoints, types.TrackedVectorCriticalPoints, locals(), True, True)\n\n        if time_steps == -1:\n            self.time_steps = self.root_node.time_steps\n        else:\n            self.time_steps = time_steps\n        self.backend = backend\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"queued tracking vector field critical points\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def description(cls):\n        return 'Tracks the locations of vector field critical points over time.'\n\n    @classmethod\n    def param_descriptions(cls):\n        return { 'parent_node_id' : 'The id of a node of type vector_cp corresponding to the points to be tracked',\n            'time_steps': 'How many time steps should the tracking be computed for. Set this equal to -1 for all time steps.',\n         'backend': 'Which backend algorithm should be used for the tracking. Choices are '\n                    'OPTIONS:tracking.'}\n\n    @classmethod\n    def mandatory_parameters(cls):\n        return [\"time_steps\", \"backend\"]\n    \n    def _evaluation_logic(self, parent_data, time_step):\n        pairing = _track_points(parent_data, self.time_steps, self.backend)\n        return types.TrackedVectorCriticalPoints(parent_data[time_step-1].points, pairing)\n    \n    def _evaluation_logic_partial_cache(self, parent_data, partial_cache, time_step):\n        partial_cache.points = parent_data.points\n        return partial_cache\n\nclass TrackSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(Node):\n\n    def __init__(self, parent_node_id : str, time_steps : int, backend : str):\n        if correctness_checks_on():\n            if backend not in options_lists[\"tracking\"]:\n                raise Exception(f\"Invalid tracking backend {backend}. Valid choices are {enumerate_list(options_lists['tracking'])}\")\n            if time_steps == 0 or time_steps < -1 or time_steps > self.root_node.time_steps:\n                raise Exception(f\"Invalid number of time steps. Must be between 1 and {self.root_node.time_steps} or -1 for all time steps.\")\n\n        super().__init__(parent_node_id, types.SymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints, types.SymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints, locals(), True, True)\n\n        if time_steps == -1:\n            self.time_steps = self.root_node.time_steps\n        else:\n            self.time_steps = time_steps\n        self.backend = backend\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"queued tracking symmetric tensor field degenerate points\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def description(cls):\n        return 'Tracks the locations of symmetric tensor field degenerate points over time.'\n\n    @classmethod\n    def param_descriptions(cls):\n        return { 'parent_node_id' : 'The id of a node of type symmetric_tensor_dp corresponding to the points being tracked',\n           'time_steps': 'How many time steps should the tracking be computed for. Set this to -1 for all time steps.',\n         'backend': 'Which backend algorithm should be used for the tracking. Choices are '\n                    'OPTIONS:tracking.'}\n\n    @classmethod\n    def mandatory_parameters(cls):\n        return [\"time_steps\", \"backend\"]\n    \n    def _evaluation_logic(self, parent_data, time_step):\n        pairing = _track_points(parent_data, self.time_steps, self.backend)\n        return types.TrackedSymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(parent_data[time_step-1].points, pairing)\n\n    def _evaluation_logic_partial_cache(self, parent_data, partial_cache, time_step):\n        partial_cache.points = parent_data.points\n        return partial_cache\n\nclass TrackAsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints(Node):\n\n    def __init__(self, parent_node_id : str, time_steps : int, backend : str):\n        if correctness_checks_on():\n            if backend not in options_lists[\"tracking\"]:\n                raise Exception(f\"Invalid tracking backend {backend}. Valid choices are {enumerate_list(options_lists['tracking'])}\")\n            if time_steps == 0 or time_steps < -1 or time_steps > self.root_node.time_steps:\n                raise Exception(f\"Invalid number of time steps. Must be between 1 and {self.root_node.time_steps} or -1 for all time steps.\")\n\n        super().__init__(parent_node_id, types.AsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints, types.AsymmetricTensorDegeneratePoints, locals(), True, True)\n\n        if time_steps == -1:\n            self.time_steps = self.root_node.time_steps\n        else:\n            self.time_steps = time_steps\n        self.backend = backend\n\n    @classmethod\n    def chat_description(cls):\n        return \"queued tracking asymmetric tensor field degenerate points\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def description(cls):\n        return 'Tracks the locations of asymmetric tensor field degenerate points over time.'\n\n    @classmethod\n    def param_descriptions(cls):\n        return { 'parent_node_id': 'The id of a node of type asymmetric_tensor_dp corresponding to the points being tracked',\n         'time_steps': 'How many time steps should the tracking be computed for. Set this to 